-- Dire Maul East (map 429): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent 11d68ad
-- (dungeons/dire_maul_east.json, status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)') with the options of the header of 20261017130000:
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 429 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev 11d68ad \
--     --stamp 20261024020300 --out <dir> dire_maul_east
-- Stacks on 20261023220000. The generator draft this replaces was never merged or applied; this is the first export. NO ROW IS HAND-SET:
-- the plan file is the source, and the fixes it carries over the generated draft are in
-- ~/TortoiseBots-audit/PREP-DIRE-MAUL-EAST-2026-10-24.md ("Fixes applied"). In short:
--   * the draft mixed five floors in every leg (courtyard z -4, south pods z -25, Zevrim's ledge z -38, basin z -52..-58, Lethtendris'
--     balcony z +16, Alzzin's cave z -120). The plan is now four legs by floor, each leg's pulls ordered by the navmesh path lengths from
--     the previous boss: 0 zevrim_thornhoof (courtyard + south pods + the basin corridor on the walk to Zevrim), 1 hydrospawn (the rest
--     of the basin), 2 lethtendris (her balcony), 3 alzzin_the_wildshaper (the cave descent and the cave). The draft's two failing look
--     points and seven detour warnings are gone: plan-check is ok, 275 points, 0 fails.
--   * the draft's leg 3 groups 7 and 8 were Gordok Brutes 11441, Mage-Lords 11444 and Mastiffs 13036 in the Gordok Commons courtyard by
--     the East wing's back door 3189 (x 293-300, y 22-40), not this wing's trash: they are out. So are leg 3 group 4 (the Isalien trigger
--     16045 plus Isalien 16097, a summoning event 6 yd from Alzzin) and leg 2 group 22 (Pimgib 14349, 3.3 yd from Lethtendris).
--   * Pimgib is Lethtendris' pet: her boss row carries first 14349. No other boss has a guard: creature_groups has no pack of a boss.
--   * every pull group is one spawn row's own creature_groups pack, at the pack's spawns; no entry and no coordinate was invented. Radii are
--     the pack's own spread plus 0.5 yd (plus the 5 yd wander for a wandering member), so a row does not reach a neighbouring pack where the
--     packs are not interleaved.
--   * the navmesh route from the courtyard to Zevrim descends the spiral through the basin: seven basin packs that stand on that walk (the
--     imps and Hellcaller at -70 -444, the rogues at -86 -463, the lashers at -31 -467, the imps at -8 -456, the Fel Lash at 50 -454, the
--     Shadowstalker at 86 -450, the trio at 70 -428) are leg 0's last pulls before him instead of being met live on the walk.
--   * patrols: 27 spawns of the wing walk (movement type 2), among them the Warpwood Treant/Stomper loops of 100-140 yd round the
--     courtyard, the two 250 yd Shadowstalker loops and the Crusher 1176392 on the cave descent. Every pull a patrol path comes within 25 yd
--     of carries a patrol block (62 of 89) with its creature_movement path and an estimated round; each single-member pull of a patrolling
--     spawn carries its own.
-- 4 legs, 318 steps, 323 rows (52 + 30 + 1 + 6 pulls; bosses 11490 Zevrim Thornhoof, 13280 Hydrospawn, 14327 Lethtendris, 11492 Alzzin the
-- Wildshaper, in leg order). Plan check (turtle-agent plan-check, map 429 mmaps): ok, 275 points, 0 fails, 62 estimated-patrol-period warnings
-- and 87 run-leader hop warnings (a pull or boss 50-100+ yd from the move row before it).
--
-- WHAT THE RUN LEADER CANNOT DO (nothing is dropped silently). Not in these rows:
--   * fleers 11454,11457 (Wildspawn Betrayer, Wildspawn Hellcaller flee at 15 % health; EventAI) and no_cc on all 17 trash entries (demons and
--     elementals: no Polymorph lands): there is no column. The plan row has cc_priority (empty: no trash is humanoid) and kill_first
--     11461,13196,11457 (the Warpwood Guardian's Regrowth-on-friendlies heal, the Phase Lasher's AoE volley phases, the Hellcaller's Fireball
--     and Rain of Fire).
--   * patrol: each pull's patrol block (entries, path, period estimate) is for the agent's driver; the run leader's rows carry no patrol, and it
--     pulls where the pack stands when it arrives. The courtyard and basin loops cannot be cleared without meeting them.
--   * the Conservatory Door 176907 (131.286 -278.89 -56.5211) blocks the way to Alzzin. It opens only through Old Ironbark's (11491) gossip,
--     and npc_ecorcefer refuses until instance data TYPE_BOSS_ZEVRIM is DONE. The plan has no gossip step: the operator opens it, or a later
--     plan adds gossip + wait_for. Zevrim is leg 0, so the order is right.
--   * Pusillin (14354) is friendly (npc_pusillin sets faction 35) until the chase; an AoE that touches him aggros every Wildspawn Imp within
--     100 yd. Old Ironbark (faction 35) and Isalien (summoned, immune until her brazier 181047 is used) are not pulled either.
--   * adds no spawn row can name: Hydrospawn summons Hydrolings (22714) at 75 %, Zevrim sacrifices a random attacker (22651) every 15-18 s,
--     Lethtendris' Shadow Bolt Volley (14887) hits the party, Alzzin's Wither (22662) is a stacking DoT.
--   * the entrance (trigger 3184, portal map 1 -3981.58 771.193 160.962, level 45), level_band 53-58 and hire_composition: the run leader
--     starts inside the instance and leads the bound party as it is.
-- The ai_dungeon_boss rows are entry-scoped, not map-scoped: map 429 holds all three Dire Maul wings, so another wing's plan rows survive.
--
-- dire_maul_east: map 429, 4 legs, 318 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_east';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_east';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'dire_maul_east';

-- Dungeon bosses of map 429 for this plan's boss steps only (the commander telemetry's boss rank; see 20261021114931_world.sql): the four
-- boss steps' entries, read from Turtle's own world data (tortoise-wow sql/base creature_template: all four are rank 1 there, so the telemetry
-- would call them 'e'). The DELETE is scoped to these entries, not the map, so another Dire Maul wing's rows on map 429 survive.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (429) AND `entry` IN (11490, 13280, 14327, 11492);
